    "body": "## Motivation\n\nThe MLX backend has no LoRA support: `MlxModelRunnerStub.initialize()` never calls `maybe_init_lora_manager`, so `model_runner.lora_manager` stays `None`. But `--enable-lora` (or `--lora-paths`) is still accepted on MLX. The server starts, and the first LoRA request reaches `Scheduler.can_schedule_lora_req`, which calls `self.tp_worker.model_runner.lora_manager.validate_lora_batch(...)` and crashes the scheduler with an `AttributeError` on `None`.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Add a `validate_mlx_server_args` resolution step next to `handle_hardware_runtime_validation`. When MLX is enabled and LoRA is requested, it raises a `ValueError` that points to the standard Torch MPS path, which does support LoRA for dense models.\n- It runs before the dummy-model return, like the other model-independent checks, and is added to the overridable hook list.\n- `--enable-lora False --lora-paths ...` still passes, since the paths are ignored in that case.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nApple M2 Max:\n\n- New `test_lora_is_rejected_at_startup` in `test/registered/unit/hardware_backend/mlx/test_runtime.py` covers `--enable-lora` and `--lora-paths`. It fails on `main` and passes with this change.\n- `SGLANG_USE_MLX=1 pytest test/registered/unit/hardware_backend/mlx`: 227 passed.\n- `test/registered/unit/server_args/test_resolution_hook_registry.py` passes.\n\nI traced the crash from the code above rather than by launching a LoRA server on MLX.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot applicable.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format checks (ruff, isort, codespell on the changed files).\n- [x] Add unit tests.\n- [x] Documentation: not applicable.\n- [x] Follow SGLang code style.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40513730856](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40513730856)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40513730631](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40513730631)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40513730798](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40513730798)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
